---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro"
import Nav from "@/sections/Nav.astro"
import Footer from "@/sections/Footer.astro"

const lastUpdated = "August 12, 2026"
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy & Asset Responsibility | NFTLox"
	description="Privacy policy and responsibility rules for using NFTLox and publishing digital assets."
	lang="en"
	canonical="https://nftlox.com/privacy"
>
	<Nav />

	<article class="container-narrow mx-auto px-6 pt-24 pb-8 sm:px-10 lg:pt-32">
		<header class="max-w-3xl">
			<p class="eyebrow">LEGAL / PRIVACY</p>
			<h1 class="type-display text-mist mt-5">Privacy &amp; asset responsibility</h1>
			<p class="type-body-lg text-mist-dim mt-7 max-w-2xl">
				This page explains what it means to publish and use digital assets through NFTLox, as well
				as the service's limitations and basic privacy rules.
			</p>
			<p class="type-label text-mist-dim mt-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
		</header>

		<div
			class="border-mist-line mt-20 grid gap-16 border-t pt-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_15rem]"
		>
			<div class="space-y-14">
				<section>
					<p class="eyebrow">01 / Scope</p>
					<h2 class="type-title text-mist mt-4">Infrastructure, not custody</h2>
					<div class="type-body text-mist-dim mt-5 space-y-4">
						<p>
							NFTLox is a protocol and infrastructure for functional digital assets. We are not a
							bank, exchange, or digital-asset custodian.
						</p>
						<p>
							When using the protocol, each person is responsible for understanding the actions they
							sign, the account they use, and the consequences of publishing or transferring an
							asset.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section>
					<p class="eyebrow">02 / Publishing</p>
					<h2 class="type-title text-mist mt-4">The publisher is responsible for the asset</h2>
					<div class="type-body text-mist-dim mt-5 space-y-4">
						<p>
							The person or entity that uploads, creates, registers, or describes a digital asset is
							responsible for that asset and all associated information.
						</p>
						<p>
							This includes having the necessary rights and permissions, not infringing third-party
							rights, not uploading illegal or misleading content, and complying with applicable
							law. NFTLox does not verify or guarantee the ownership, authenticity, value, utility,
							or legality of any published asset.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section>
					<p class="eyebrow">03 / Loss &amp; transactions</p>
					<h2 class="type-title text-mist mt-4">Transactions may be irreversible</h2>
					<div class="type-body text-mist-dim mt-5 space-y-4">
						<p>
							Transactions recorded on a blockchain network may be permanent and cannot always be
							cancelled, reversed, or recovered.
						</p>
						<p>
							Users assume the risk of losing access to their account or keys, sending an asset to
							the wrong address, interacting with a third-party application, publishing data by
							mistake, or experiencing a network interruption. NFTLox cannot recover keys, reverse
							transactions, or guarantee the continuous availability of an external network or
							service.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section>
					<p class="eyebrow">04 / Acceptable use</p>
					<h2 class="type-title text-mist mt-4">Prohibited content and conduct</h2>
					<div class="type-body text-mist-dim mt-5 space-y-4">
						<p>
							NFTLox may not be used for fraud, impersonation, money laundering, sanctions evasion,
							malware, child exploitation, deliberate infringement of rights, or any illegal
							activity.
						</p>
						<p>
							We may limit, suspend, or remove an interface, account, or content when necessary to
							protect the protocol, comply with the law, or respond to abuse. This does not mean we
							can delete information already recorded on a blockchain.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section>
					<p class="eyebrow">05 / Privacy</p>
					<h2 class="type-title text-mist mt-4">Information you share</h2>
					<div class="type-body text-mist-dim mt-5 space-y-4">
						<p>
							You should avoid including unnecessary personal information in asset names,
							descriptions, metadata, or public content. Information published on a blockchain may
							be publicly visible and difficult to remove.
						</p>
						<p>
							If a third-party application or service processes your data, that processing may be
							subject to its own privacy policy. This page does not replace the policies of those
							third parties.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section>
					<p class="eyebrow">06 / Changes &amp; contact</p>
					<h2 class="type-title text-mist mt-4">A policy that may evolve</h2>
					<div class="type-body text-mist-dim mt-5 space-y-4">
						<p>
							We may update this policy to reflect changes to the protocol, services, or law. The
							updated date will appear at the beginning of this page.
						</p>
						<p>
							For questions about this policy or to report abuse, contact the NFTLox team through
							the official channels linked on the site.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>
			</div>

			<nav class="hidden lg:block" aria-label="On this page">
				<p class="type-label text-citrus">On this page</p>
				<ul class="type-ui text-mist-dim border-mist-line mt-4 space-y-3 border-l pl-4">
					<li>Scope</li>
					<li>Publishing</li>
					<li>Loss</li>
					<li>Acceptable use</li>
					<li>Privacy</li>
				</ul>
			</nav>
		</div>
	</article>

	<Footer />
</Layout>
